Third-party notices — myne-clipper
==================================

Copyright (C) 2026 Myne contributors.

The shipped artefact is the extension bundle in `dist/` (`pnpm build`). The
bundler runs with `bundle: true`, so a runtime dependency is INLINED into
`background.js`, `content.js` and `popup.js` rather than resolved from a package
manager when the browser loads the extension. The browsers each apply their own
review policy to a packaged extension, and every one of them expects a bundled
dependency's licence to travel with it, which is why `scripts/build.mjs` copies
the file below into `dist/` next to the bundles.


Bundled runtime dependency
--------------------------

  webextension-polyfill  0.12.0  ·  Mozilla Public License 2.0
    Author   Mozilla and contributors
    Source   https://github.com/mozilla/webextension-polyfill
    Text     dist/LICENSE.webextension-polyfill.txt

    MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft. It obliges us to make the source of the
    MPL-covered files available, which the unmodified upstream package already
    satisfies, and it imposes no condition on the AGPL-3.0-only work that bundles it
    — which is why the extension can be AGPL-3.0-only and this file can be MPL-2.0 at
    the same time.

    The text is COPIED by the build rather than transcribed here, so what ships
    is the licence of the version that was actually inlined. A hand-copied
    licence is the copy that goes stale on a bump, silently, because nothing
    reads it.

    Measured on 0.12.0, its LICENSE is MPL-2.0. The main repo's
    `scripts/check-npm-licenses.mjs` allowlist already carries MPL-2.0.


Build-time only, not redistributed
----------------------------------

  esbuild (MIT)          bundles this extension. It is a build tool: its own
                         source is not in `dist/`. The small runtime helpers it
                         emits into a bundle are covered by its licence, and it
                         emits none of them here (`format: "iife"`, no decorators,
                         no `import.meta` rewriting).
  typescript (Apache-2.0), vitest (MIT), jsdom (MIT)   development tools
  @types/firefox-webext-browser (MIT)                  declaration-only, no bytes


How to verify the scope
-----------------------

  pnpm build && ls dist/
  node -e "console.log(Object.keys(require('./package.json').dependencies))"

`tests/notice.test.ts` holds the first of those two facts to the second: a
dependency added to `package.json` without a row here fails the suite.
